<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20749" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βράβῠλος</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the tree which bears</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βράβυλα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CA</u>
				2.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				10.39
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βράβυλον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.377
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Pall.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>seedling peach,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gp.
				10.13.5
			</span></i>. (The forms <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βράβιλος,
			βράβηλος</span> are found in codd. of <u>Gp.</u> and
				<u>AP</u>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βράβηλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>EM</u>
					211.3
				</span></i>
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βράβιλον</span> codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
